 {:seon.task/name "a-debug-view-of-any-agent"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-23: \"Lets get the web UI working better so I can get a debug view into any agent.\" Replaces a-turn-is-a-row-on-the-agent-page (its proof included). What exists: /agent/{id} (seon.render.ui/agent-page: zoom-head, zoom-work, proofs-box, the newest context read in zoom-context, the evaluations as history entries), built by seon.render.proc's zoom-value from root's view entry, main's run and the agent's branch db. It shows no turn: a model call's facts (:seon.model-call/fact: reply, reasoning, tokens, cache hits, split, basis) have no render; it shows only the newest context; an agent root no longer holds (a kept run, another boot) has an empty page; there is no way to message the agent (parity entry 73) or release its held task. v1 (~/src/seon/src/seon/render/web.clj debug-response, sent.clj view): /agent/{id}/debug lists each model call (prompt, cached and completion tokens, finish) and opens it into what it was sent, remade from the call's basis (never stored), its sections token-badged; /agent/{id}/message writes a :seon.message fact the next turn's current-state block shows as unread. As built (owner, 2026-10-23: \"show useful data, not all the data\"; \"It's all just functions and results\"): renders are functions of a value and its opts, (render v opts) with :as (:inline, :block, :tile), :budget, :handle, :schema, :unit and :face as props, an :html render answering hiccup and an :ai render {:text :truncated?}; a hiccup vector headed by a function is a call (Reagent's form, seon.web.html/write!); the printer shows a nested value with a declared render by that render, both faces (seon.render/nested). The agent's window, /agent/{id} and /run/{id} (stable across boots), is chat-style: (1) the head says why the agent is as it is (seon.render.ui/why, zoom-head: one sentence, its run, branch, model, process, times, model turns apart from reads, tokens and cost at the model's prices, seon.model/cost); (2) the conversation, each turn and each evaluation outside the turns its own unit appended in write order: a turn's header (turn n of max, its id), what it was told, its reasoning and reply, then per call its thinking (the eval tool's argument) and per form its ;; thought (seon.reader/lead, the record's :lead), the form and its result (the records the call names by :items); its tokens, time and proofs as it began; and the context it read, made again from its basis (seon.context/remade), the whole request at /turn?view=&id=; (3) the input at the bottom: a send evaluates (seon.root/submit!), one starting > is a message (seon.root/message!), interrupt and release beside it; (4) the right column of tiles, each its own unit renumbered on change so the last changed is first: the task, the proofs, the branch (:will-merge, conflicts) and the problems. Messages are facts: root writes :seon.message/* on main, from \"owner\" to the run, and the turn that takes it writes the same fact on its branch and names it by id in its basis (seon.turn/basis!), read by seon.context/taken-messages; an observer's read of a model-driven agent leaves the inbox. An ended agent's window reads its run on main and its branch from the store. Live by events (a commit event, root's view changing), never polled. Deletes zoom-context's one-read panel, the runs table on the page and the agent's card tile. Not done: another agent's sends as facts; /ns/{ns} and /data (task namespace-agent-debug-and-data-pages). Superseded by seon.render/page (2026-10-23): every page is an entity's walk laid out by seon.render.ui/page, and its proofs are that task's."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.render-test/the-printer-renders-each-nested-value-by-its-own-render seon.render-cost-test/render-calls-are-one-pass-over-their-nodes seon.render-cost-test/the-printer-renders-nested-values-in-one-pass seon.render-cost-test/main-info-reads-what-the-page-shows seon.context-test/an-owners-message-reaches-the-next-turn seon.context-test/a-taken-message-is-read-from-its-fact seon.agent-test/a-model-turn-records-its-prose-and-the-message-it-took seon.repl-test/a-forms-lead-is-recorded-with-its-eval seon.web-test/a-vector-headed-by-a-function-is-a-call seon.server-test/a-message-reaches-the-agent seon.model-test/cost-prices-a-turn-at-its-models-rates seon.render-test/a-units-change-rerenders-that-unit}}
