 {:seon.task/name "namespace-agent-debug-and-data-pages"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `seon.web/handler` serves /, /agent/{id}, /feed, /context.txt, /render.edn, /web.edn and POST /call; pages are ``seon.render.ui/system-page`` and ``seon.render.ui/agent-page``. v1's route table (~/src/seon/src/seon/render/route.clj) also served /ns/{namespace} and /ns/{namespace}/debug, /agent/{id}/debug and /data (docs/parity.md). Missing: the owner cannot see a namespace's vars, contracts and the tests reaching them, an agent's raw records, or main's data. Correct: each a view the render proc renders from main's or the agent's branch, through renders declared on the values' schemas (docs/render.md), routed beside /agent/; read first what each v1 page showed and keep what the owner acts on (seon.render/the-page-shows-only-what-acts). Replaces nothing."
