 {:seon.task/name "a-page-part-renders-only-its-view"
  :seon.task/plan "Step 1 of docs/render.md (revision 3): delete first. What exists: every page part (`seon.render.ui/row`, `tile`, `head`) is drawn through `seon.render/shown`, which renders the part's :ai face beside its :html face and records which render made each (`seon.render/render-name`), on every pass of root's render proc; nothing reads the :ai face, its text or the makers (the archived paper audit-2026-10-24.md (git history) correction 1). `seon.render/rendered` and `seon.render/data` are read only by tests. `seon.screen/show` hand-builds a page in the agent's process from its in-memory state, a second producer of the agent's view (design section 10). Reuses: `seon.render/html`, the one :html render call, at the three part sites. Deletes: `shown`, `rendered`, `data`, `render-name` and their schema keys (:seon.render/shown, ai-by, html-by, ai-text, truncated?, the walk's tests of them), `seon.screen/show` and `cited` with the `(seon.screen/show)` screen form (the screen keeps `(my.task/status)` and `(my.branch/changes)` until step 4 makes it a read of root's cached page). Adds nothing. Proofs: a page part whose value declares an :ai render that throws still renders (red before: shown called it); the page tests stay green; the context test's screen is the two forms."
