 {:seon.task/name "a-view-renders-once-per-change-of-its-reads"
  :seon.task/plan "Step 2 of docs/render.md (revision 3), the foundation; design section 3 (Render each thing once; Components, reads and patches) and root's research (datahike-reads.md). Four parts, each merged with its proofs.
(A) Read recording in the Datahike fork, branch jolt/with-reads of seantempesta/datahike (pinned at reference-code/datahike, today 698a2faf). Reuses the one index interface every read bottoms out in (IIndex, index/persistent_set.cljc -slice, -rslice, -lookup; -all, -seq, -count record a wildcard). Adds a dynamic collector `*reads*` there (one vswap! a range, [index from to] as the slice is made, so laziness after the call is fine); db/search.cljc memoize-for and the query result cache bypassed while recording (both off on root today); `datahike.query/*disable-planner*` bound while recording (the planner's ~25 cursor calls skip the interface; the relational engine is faster on point and 2-hop queries, 2.6x slower on a join of 392 tuples). API in datahike.api: `(d/with-reads f)` answers [result reads]; `(d/reads-index reads)` keys each range by its bound prefix ([:e e] [:ea e a] [:a a] [:av a v], or any); `(d/reads-touched? idx tx-data)` one hash lookup a datom, added or retracted, a schema datom touching all. Deletes nothing. ~35 lines, Datahike's tests beside them. Proofs (fork): with-reads records 3 ranges for a pull with one nested ref, 1 for a unique point query, 1 for an attribute scan; reads-touched? is true for a datom in a read range and false outside it, for an addition and a retraction; cost: reads-touched? costs the transaction's datoms, flat in the number of reads.
(B) One render cache keyed by reads, in seon.render.proc (its state, no new namespace), whose components are today's pages, one per db a page reads (root's ruling 2026-10-24, option 2: per-entity components are step 4's, task a-page-is-its-entitys-view, on this cache): each watched page's walk on main and on its agent's branch runs inside d/with-reads, and the page keeps each db's reads index; an inverted index per db (key -> views, from d/datom-keys) finds the pages a transaction touched in O(its datoms). A touched page walks again and its units re-render only when their input changed (step-units' comparison stays until step 4). Reuses render/page, step-units, finish-patch. Deletes nothing yet. ~50 lines. Proofs: seon.render-test/a-page-keeps-what-it-read (a page's reads hold its entity and its members' entities; a datom of another entity is not among them).
(C) Root's render proc walks and renders only the pages a transaction touched. Main: the writer's report, connected [:writer :main] -> [:render :main] ({:t :ops :db}, as the reconciler, prove and vectors take it), replacing the :state answer's tx-count compare and its :branch-db ask for main. An agent's branch: its :commit event (exists) asks the branch db as today (ask-branches), and the datoms that moved are (d/datoms-diff held new :eavt []) (O(changed), as merge.clj and program.clj use it). Deletes: the pass that walks every watched page per event: an event or transaction touching no page's reads walks and renders nothing. Root's system value and its :ai context stay a pass per state answer (not a page; out of this step). ~40 lines changed. Proofs: seon.render-test/a-transaction-touching-no-page-walks-nothing, seon.render-test/a-branch-commit-touches-its-page-by-its-datoms-diff; cost: seon.render-cost-test/a-transaction-costs-its-datoms-to-match (finding the touched pages: linear in the datoms, flat in the pages watched).
(D) Agents commit after each eval: seon.turn/act!'s call loop commits (seon.agent/commit!) after each call's record, so a page sees an eval as it lands (design section 11 item 1, approved). Reuses commit! (no-op when nothing waits); the commit at idle and turn end stays (it covers writes outside an eval). ~3 lines. Proof: seon.agent-test/an-agent-commits-after-each-eval (process test: two calls, two :commit events before the turn's end). Measured: a commit's cost (ticks, bytes) per eval, before and after, reported with the step; if it is past the eval's own cost, root decides before merging.
What it does not do: per-entity components and the agent page and screen as views (step 4, task a-page-is-its-entitys-view), recording what a turn sent (step 3), the browser's lazy placeholders (design section 4). Estimated src: +~90 (fork ~65 outside src), -~30. Checked in a browser: root's page and an agent's page update as an agent evaluates, with the render proc's counts showing hits."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.render/a-page-part-renders-only-its-view"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{datahike.reads-test/a-read-records-what-it-scanned
                      datahike.reads-test/a-transaction-touches-only-what-a-read-scanned
                      datahike.reads-test/a-read-inside-a-flow-step-is-recorded
                      datahike.reads-test/a-transaction-costs-its-datoms-to-match
                      datahike.reads-test/matching-is-flat-in-what-was-read
                      seon.render-test/a-page-keeps-what-it-read
                      seon.render-test/a-transaction-touching-no-page-walks-nothing
                      seon.render-test/a-branch-commit-touches-its-page-by-its-datoms-diff
                      seon.render-cost-test/a-transaction-costs-its-datoms-to-match
                      seon.agent-test/an-agent-commits-after-each-eval}}
